{
 "id": "CACHE-14-bar-states",
 "note": "0.1.13: `cache --bar` is the status-line meter, one golden per state: 12 cells and a suffix, fill and age from the expiry only (fill = (ttl - seconds_left) / ttl, age = now - (expires_at - ttl)), so a fork's read that moves expires_at but not the last main request reads by the expiry. Unknown and a null TTL print nothing; `~` marks a TTL read from the transcript; keep-warm warming shows n/max and ↻, `…` while a ping is out, ` off` only when keep-warm refused the gap near a usage limit; cold is full with its age or `cold miss`; compacted is empty cells. --color never here; colours are CACHE-15.",
 "now": "2026-11-09T12:00:00Z",
 "tz": "UTC",
 "steps": [
  {
   "name": "unknown (no stdin, no state): nothing, exit 0",
   "argv": [
    "cache",
    "--stdin",
    "--bar",
    "--color",
    "never"
   ],
   "expect": {
    "exit": 0,
    "stdout": "",
    "stderr_empty": true
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "unknown, a session's first refresh (no prompt_cache, no transcript): nothing",
